      "writtenOn": "2025-10-20T18:36:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a case where Chrome might have an EGL context current that Dawn might not know about? If I\u0027m understanding the purpose, it seems like eglGetCurrentContext() might be safer than attempting to track it ourselves.",
      "revId": "4ac5b5cbe8ed5fb180fa7b8e8bf94c9da2f8370e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0ef0df2_b5b5a017",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/DeviceGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 526,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-22T13:54:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could use `eglGetCurrentContext` in future, I have added a TODO for that. It\u0027s unsafe to use it currently because there are two ways the context would be made current: `DeprecatedMakeCurrent` and `ScopedMakeCurrent`. Ideally we should use `ScopedMakeCurrent` everywhere. But it\u0027s a iterative effort.\n\nLet\u0027s say we used `eglGetCurrentContext` and this call sequence happened:\n- No current context.\n- Buffer.Map().\n- Buffer.Unmap().\n  - Use `AddGLWork()` to schedule a buffer upload.\n- Some legacy code uses `DeprecatedMakeCurrent`.\n- Buffer.Destroy()\n  - Use `AddGLWork()` to schedule a buffer destroy.\n  - Because the condition `eglGetCurrentContext() \u003d\u003d context` is true. The buffer is destroyed immediately.\n- `Queue.Submit()`\n  - `ExecutePendingGLWork()`:\n    - buffer upload is executed. But the buffer is already destroyed -\u003e error.\n    \nThe current thread local tracking ensures that the order of deferred tasks are guaranteed within `ExecutePendingGLWork()` only.",
      "parentUuid": "d0a324d3_6378e7f2",
      "revId": "4ac5b5cbe8ed5fb180fa7b8e8bf94c9da2f8370e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
